    "lore": "Hesketh Vane was a Tallymen's clerk at the salt-gate who saw that a Tallyman looks at a seal and not at a mountain, and went round the back with a spade. Six years of tunnels later he holds court in the Saltmound's heart on a throne of the Charter's own sacks, with a crown of salt crystals grown on a wire and a Hushed sayer's tricks he bought at the Dumb Fair, and the Free Salters call him King because he pays. He is courteous to everyone and generous to his people and he will not give back a grain.",
